Meh.  personally out of that lot I would pick Magicbane for
a Tourist -- not because it kills things fast (it doesn't), but
for its other benefits:  instant engraving, backup source
of slotless MR (in case the Wiz or a nymph makes off
with the PYEC), and partial curse blocking.

For killing things fast, alchemize some potions of gain
level and find some attack-spell books.  Tourists have
a base spellcasting penalty of only 5 -- only wizards,
priests, and healers have a lower base penalty, and
Monks have a higher one (although they get a better
bonus from wearing a robe).

Also, carry a handful of attack wands and invoke
the platinum card every couple of hundred turns.
Almost all monsters are vulnerable to one form
of attack wand or another.

> > - no Vorpy, Mjollnir or a handful of others

You don't need those.  Vorpy is only just *barely*
better than a non-artifact longsword.  (Yeah, yeah,
beheading sounds like it would be all kinds of
cool, but it happens too small a percentage of
the time to matter very much in actual practice.)
If you've seen too many artifacts to wish up a
real superweapon, Magicbane will do in a pinch.
#twoweapon it with a silver saber (in Gehennom)
or any good non-artifact weapon (elsewhere).

