Indeed:  if you *don't* want to get crowned, you should not
pray for holy water after the early middle game.  Just save
your last holy water and dip a large stack of uncursed water
(20 or so at a time is good -- the more you do at once, the
fewer potions you waste by using up one each time) in it to
make a new batch of holy water.  This has the added benefit
of not requiring an altar, so if your only co-aligned altar is far
away (like, in Minetown) and you don't want to risk trying to
convert one, this can save you an extra trip.

But if you're trying to get crowned, go ahead and pray for
the holy water whenever you need some; you might also
get crowned in the process, and there's no downside.


